From 62ff27237e2a1ccc1bc467caf7966224f5d965d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:43:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(post): per-operation coolant - off, flood, mist or
 through tool

Each operation now carries a coolant choice (Operation.coolant, the post
crate's CoolantMode), default Flood - what every built-in post already
switched on per section - so all CL/NC goldens stay byte-exact.

- Stream: flood is the silent default; any other choice rides one
  PARAM Coolant off|mist|through-tool ahead of the section.
- Posts (Fanuc, Haas, Siemens 840D, Heidenhain, Mazak, Fanuc Lathe):
  coolantFor() takes the mounted machine's own code for the family
  (Flood / Mist / Through-spindle or Through-tool); M9 still closes
  every section before M5, so coolant is off across tool changes and
  at program end; a dry section writes neither word. A choice the
  machine states no code for is a counted message() - the gate blocks
  the post by name instead of cutting dry.
- Command: EditOperationParams::with_coolant, one undo unit; the stamp
  survives (coolant shapes no geometry).
- UI: a Coolant row under Tool in the op page header grid
  (CommandKind::EditOperationCoolant).
- Project file: "coolant" written only off the default; absent reads
  Flood, so older files load and round-trip unchanged.
- Shell snapshots (egui_app.png / egui_app_light.png) updated: the op
  page gains the Coolant row.

Fixes #112

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
