From 45a020f4e199be95716eb23c6de66d86873b9ad0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:21:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(post): coolant refusals name the op; no flood code,
 no silent dry cut

Follow-ups from the coolant review (PR #147):

- Every built-in post captures the section's OperationName and prefixes
  its coolant message() with "operation <name>:", so a multi-op program
  says which op asked for the code the machine lacks.
- A Flood op on a machine whose coolant list states only other kinds
  (Mist, Through-spindle) is refused by name, never posted as M7 or dry.
  A shop's own name (Brine) is still its flood; an unstated list and a
  codeless Flood entry stay silent (the unstated-limit law).
- Coolant names compare trimmed, case-blind, spaces/underscores as
  hyphens, so "Through spindle" reads; the machine editor picks from
  machine::COOLANT_KINDS (Flood, Mist, Through-spindle, Through-tool)
  plus a custom text name. Machine and post docs list the names.
- Post capability flag coolantModes = true (every shipped post sets it):
  the engine refuses, by op name, any PARAM Coolant reaching a script
  without it, so a user post that ignores the word cannot flood an
  Off/Mist/Through-tool op.
- Owed tests: Fanuc Lathe per-section coolant, M88 on the shipped
  mill-turn, the op page dropdown click path, Mist then Flood on every
  mill post (coolant_followups.rs, coolant_tests.rs).

Default-Flood goldens unchanged (conformance green).

Fixes #150

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
